Rast wrote:
> Doug Freyburger wrote:
>
>> Also experiment with
>> other types of armor and what they do to your spell casting. 
>
> Doug means, I think, types of armor that go in other slots: boots, 
> helmet, gloves, cloak, shield.  When it comes to body armor, there are 
> only three real choices:
> - leather/studded leather for casters
> - dwarf/elf mithril for non-casters
> - dragon scale mail for everyone, when available

Agreed but I did not limit my meaning to that.  It a few turns trying on
non-studded leather, splint, banded or plate armor to figure out that
either studded leather or mithril beat them for wizards.

For that matter because of the weight I often use mithril for my fighter
class games until I can get dragon scales.

There are 3 AC points difference between studded leather and mithril. 
If your only armor is body armor that's a lot.  But add high boots and
leather gloves and those 3 points are covered.  It's not all that hard
to figure out which armor types have little or no interference with
spell casting and end up with a set that justifies switching from
mithril to studded leather.


